text:
Pasal 2
Azas (1) Perlindungan perempuan dan anak berdasarkan Pancasila  dan Undang-Undang Dasar Negara Republik Indonesia  Tahun 1945 serta prinsip-prinsip dan hak dasar  sebagaimana diatur dalam Konvensi Perempuan dan  Anak, meliputi :
a. penghormatan atas hak asasi manusia;
b. non-diskriminasi;
c. kepentingan yang terbaik bagi perempuan dan/atau  anak;
d. hak untuk hidup, kelangsungan hidup dan  berkembang;
e. penghargaan terhadap pendapat perempuan dan anak; f. kesetaraan dan keadilan gender; dan
g. perlindungan korban;
(2) Kepastian Hukum dan Kearifan lokal.

translated_text:
Article 2
Principles (1) The protection of women and children is based on Pancasila and the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia as well as the principles and basic rights as regulated in the Convention on Women and Children, including:
a. respect for human rights;
b. non-discrimination;
c. the best interests of women and/or children;
d. the right to life, survival and development;
e. respect for the opinions of women and children; f. gender equality and justice; and
g. protection of victims;
(2) Legal Certainty and Local Wisdom.

text:
Pasal 3
Tujuan Tujuan perlindungan perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan  adalah:
a. menjamin terpenuhinya hak-hak perempuan dan/atau  anak sesuai ketentuan yang berlaku;
b. mencegah dan melindungi perempuan dan/atau anak dari  tindak kekerasan;
c. mendorong masyarakat untuk melaksanakan  kewajibannya dalam pencegahan dan perlindungan terhadap perempuan dan anak sesuai ketentuan  Perundang-undangan yang berlaku; dan
d. memulihkan korban dari akibat tindak kekerasan yang  dialami.

translated_text:
Article 3
Objectives The objectives of protection for women and children victims of violence are:
a. to guarantee the fulfillment of the rights of women and/or children in accordance with applicable provisions;
b. to prevent and protect women and/or children from acts of violence;
c. to encourage the community to carry out its obligations in the prevention and protection of women and children in accordance with applicable legislative provisions; and
d. to restore victims from the consequences of acts of violence experienced.

text:
Pasal 4
Ruang Lingkup Ruang lingkup penyelenggaraan perlindungan terhadap  perempuan dan anak Korban Kekerasan meliputi:
a. kelembagaan penyelenggaraan perlindungan terhadap  perempuan dan anak;
b. tugas dan tanggung jawab pencegahan, perlindungan dan  pemulihan;
c. bentuk dan mekanisme pencegahan; dan
d. penyediaan layanan medis, medikolegal, ruang  pemeriksaan khusus, bantuan hukum, tenaga ahli,  pemulihan psikologis, rumah aman, pendamping sosial,  rohaniwan, dukungan pranata adat, pemulangan,  reintegrasi sosial, pemberdayaan ekonomi dan layanan  lainnya yang dibutuhkan perempuan dan anak korban  kekerasan untuk mendukung pemenuhan hak perempuan  dan anak korban kekerasan.

translated_text:
Article 4
Scope The scope of implementation of protection for women and children Victims of Violence includes:
a. institutional implementation of protection for women and children;
b. duties and responsibilities for prevention, protection and recovery;
c. forms and mechanisms of prevention; and
d. provision of medical services, medicolegal, special examination rooms, legal assistance, expert personnel, psychological recovery, safe houses, social companions, religious counselors, support of customary institutions, repatriation, social reintegration, economic empowerment and other services needed by women and children victims of violence to support the fulfillment of the rights of women and children victims of violence.

text:
BAB II
HAK-HAK KORBAN
Pasal 5
Korban berhak mendapatkan:
a. perlindungan dari pihak keluarga, Pemerintah Daerah,  kepolisian, kejaksaan, pengadilan, lembaga bantuan  hukum, lembaga sosial atau pihak lainnya baik sementara  maupun berdasarkan penetapan perintah perlindungan  dari pengadilan;
b. penanganan secara khusus berkaitan dengan keamanan  dan kerahasiaan korban;
c. layanan kesehatan fisik, psikis dan layanan psikologis  sesuai penderitaan yang dialami korban;
d. pendampingan oleh pekerja sosial dan bantuan hukum  pada setiap tingkat proses pemeriksaan sesuai dengan  ketentuan Peraturan Perundang-undangan;
e. layanan bimbingan rohani; dan
f. jaminan keberlangsungan pendidikan khusus bagi anak  yang menjadi korban kekerasan.

translated_text:
CHAPTER II
RIGHTS OF VICTIMS
Article 5
Victims have the right to obtain:
a. protection from family members, Regional Government, police, prosecution, court, legal aid institutions, social institutions or other parties either temporarily or based on the determination of a protection order from the court;
b. special handling related to the security and confidentiality of victims;
c. physical health services, mental health services and psychological services in accordance with the suffering experienced by victims;
d. assistance by social workers and legal aid at every level of the examination process in accordance with the provisions of Laws and Regulations;
e. spiritual guidance services; and
f. guarantee of continuity of education specifically for children who become victims of violence.

text:
Pasal 8
(1) Tugas dan tanggung jawab Pemerintah Daerah sebagaimana  dimaksud dalam Pasal 7 huruf a, meliputi:
a. melaksanakan kebijakan perlindungan perempuan dan  anak dari tindak kekerasan yang ditetapkan oleh  pemerintah;
b. menetapkan kebijakan, program dan kegiatan perlindungan  perempuan dan anak dari tindak kekerasan;
c. melakukan kerja sama dalam penyelenggaraan  perlindungan perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan;
d. memberikan dukungan sarana dan prasarana pelaksanaan  perlindungan perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan  kepada instansi terkait baik vertikal maupun daerah;
e. mengalokasikan anggaran perlindungan perempuan dan  anak korban kekerasan sesuai kemampuan keuangan  Daerah; dan
f. membina dan mengawasi penyelenggaraan perlindungan  perempuan dan anak dari tindak kekerasan.
(2) Dalam rangka melaksanakan kewajiban dan tanggung jawab  Pemerintah Daerah sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1),  Bupati menetapkan program dan kegiatan aksi perlindungan  perempuan dan anak dalam suatu rencana aksi Daerah.
(3) Rencana aksi Daerah sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (2)  merupakan bagian dari Rencana Pembangunan Jangka  Menengah Daerah.
(4) Ketentuan lebih lanjut mengenai Rencana Aksi Daerah  sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (2) diatur dengan Peraturan  Bupati.

translated_text:
Article 8
(1) The duties and responsibilities of the Regional Government as referred to in Article 7 letter a, include:
a. implementing policies for the protection of women and children from acts of violence established by the government;
b. establishing policies, programs and activities for the protection of women and children from acts of violence;
c. conducting cooperation in the implementation of protection of women and children victims of violence;
d. providing support for facilities and infrastructure for the implementation of protection of women and children victims of violence to related agencies both vertical and regional;
e. allocating budget for the protection of women and children victims of violence in accordance with the financial capacity of the Region; and
f. fostering and supervising the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence.
(2) In order to carry out the obligations and responsibilities of the Regional Government as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regent establishes programs and action activities for the protection of women and children in a regional action plan.
(3) The regional action plan as referred to in paragraph (2) constitutes part of the Regional Medium-Term Development Plan.
(4) Further provisions regarding the Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

text:
Pasal 9
Kewajiban dan tanggung jawab masyarakat sebagaimana  dimaksud dalam Pasal 7 huruf b, meliputi:
a. mencegah terjadinya tindak kekerasan terhadap perempuan  dan anak;
b. memberikan perlindungan terhadap korban;
c. memberikan pertolongan darurat;
d. memberikan informasi dan/atau melaporkan tindak  kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak kepada pihak  yang berwenang; dan
e. turut serta dalam penanganan korban kekerasan.

translated_text:
Article 9
The obligations and responsibilities of the community as referred to in Article 7 letter b, include:
a. preventing the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children;
b. providing protection to victims;
c. providing emergency assistance;
d. providing information and/or reporting acts of violence against women and children to the competent authorities; and
e. participating in the handling of victims of violence.

text:
Pasal 16
P2TP2A berkewajiban untuk:
a. memberikan layanan dan penanganan secepat mungkin  kepada korban;
b. memberikan kemudahan dan kenyamanan layanan bagi  korban;
c. memberikan layanan secara cuma-cuma bagi korban; d. menjaga keamanan dan kerahasiaan korban; dan
e. mengupayakan tercapainya keadilan dan kepastian hukum  bagi korban.

translated_text:
Article 16
P2TP2A has the obligation to:
a. provide services and handling as quickly as possible to victims;
b. provide ease and comfort of services for victims;
c. provide services free of charge for victims; d. maintain the security and confidentiality of victims; and
e. strive for the achievement of justice and legal certainty for victims.

text:
Pasal 17
Pencegahan terjadinya tindak kekerasan terhadap perempuan  dan anak dapat dilaksanakan melalui:
a. sosialisasi Peraturan Perundang-Undangan kepada  masyarakat berkaitan dengan perlindungan perempuan dan  anak secara berkala;
b. kampanye 16 Hari Anti Kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan  anak setiap tahun;
c. mengintegrasi isu kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak  ke dalam kurikulum pendidikan di sekolah;
d. penyelenggaraan mekanisme rujukan dalam penanganan  dan pemulihan korban kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan  anak; dan
e. koordinasi antar institusi yang memiliki tugas pokok dan fungsi yang terkait dengan pencegahan dan penanganan  kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak.

translated_text:
Article 17
Prevention of the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children can be implemented through:
a. socialization of Laws and Regulations to the community related to the protection of women and children on a regular basis;
b. campaign of 16 Days of Anti-Violence against women and children every year;
c. integrating issues of violence against women and children into the education curriculum in schools;
d. implementation of referral mechanisms in the handling and recovery of victims of violence against women and children; and
e. coordination between institutions that have main duties and functions related to the prevention and handling of violence against women and children.

text:
Pasal 19
(1) Pencegahan tindak kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan  anak sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 17 dan Pasal 18,  dilaksanakan oleh organisasi perangkat daerah sesuai tugas  dan fungsi di bidang:
a. pemberdayaan perempuan dan perlindungan anak;  b. kesehatan;
c. mental dan spiritual;
d. sosial;
e. pendidikan;
f. ketenagakerjaan; dan
g. ketenteraman dan ketertiban.
(2) Pencegahan tindak kekerasan oleh satuan kerja perangkat  daerah sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilaksanakan  berdasarkan Rencana Aksi Daerah.

translated_text:
Article 19
(1) Prevention of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in Article 17 and Article 18, shall be implemented by regional apparatus organizations in accordance with their duties and functions in the fields of:
a. women's empowerment and child protection;
b. health;
c. mental and spiritual;
d. social;
e. education;
f. employment; and
g. peace and order.
(2) Prevention of acts of violence by regional apparatus work units as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented based on the Regional Action Plan.

text:
Pasal 20
(1) Layanan bagi korban diselenggarakan secara bekerjasama  antar lembaga/institusi terkait, meliputi
a. layanan hukum berupa bantuan hukum dan  pendampingan paralegal;
b. layanan medis;
c. layanan medikolegal;
d. layanan psikologis;
e. layanan rehabilitasi;
f. layanan reintegrasi sosial dan pemulangan; dan g. layanan dukungan untuk kemandirian ekonomi.
(2) Koordinasi layanan bagi korban sebagaimana dimaksud  pada ayat (1) dilakukan oleh P2TP2A.

translated_text:
Article 20
(1) Services for victims are organized through cooperation among related agencies/institutions, including
a. legal services in the form of legal aid and paralegal assistance;
b. medical services;
c. medicolegal services;
d. psychological services;
e. rehabilitation services;
f. social reintegration and repatriation services; and g. support services for economic independence.
(2) Coordination of services for victims as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by P2TP2A.

text:
Pasal 24
(1) Pemerintah Daerah berkewajiban melakukan pemberdayaan  terhadap perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan.
(2) Pemberdayaan korban sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1),  dengan melibatkan P2TP2A.
(3) Dalam melakukan pemberdayaan perempuan korban  kekerasan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1), Pemerintah  Daerah menyusun program pemberdayaan di bidang  ekonomi, yang meliputi:
a. mengusahakan kebutuhan yang diperlukan bagi  pelatihan kewirausahaan terhadap perempuan korban  kekerasan guna meningkatkan pengetahuan, sikap dan  ketrampilan berusaha;
b. memfasilitasi terlaksananya berbagai pelatihan kerja  dan pelatihan ketrampilan;
c. melakukan pendampingan dalam mengembangkan  usaha ekonomi;
d. menjajaki kerjasama dengan perusahaan kecil,  menengah dan besar, serta lembaga keuangan untuk  mengembangkan usaha perempuan korban tindak  kekerasan;
e. mengupayakan penyediaan modal bagi perempuan  korban tindak kekerasan; dan
f. memperluas akses informasi dan mempromosikan hasil  produk perempuan korban tindak kekerasan.
(4) Dalam melakukan pemberdayaan perempuan korban  kekerasan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1), Pemerintah  Daerah dapat menjalin kerjasama dengan lembaga pelatihan  kerja yang diselenggarakan oleh swasta.

translated_text:
Article 24
(1) The Regional Government is obligated to conduct empowerment of women and children victims of violence.
(2) Empowerment of victims as referred to in paragraph (1), by involving P2TP2A.
(3) In conducting empowerment of women victims of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government shall formulate empowerment programs in the economic field, which include:
a. providing the necessary requirements for entrepreneurship training for women victims of violence in order to increase knowledge, attitudes and business skills;
b. facilitating the implementation of various job training and skills training;
c. providing assistance in developing economic enterprises;
d. exploring cooperation with small, medium and large companies, as well as financial institutions to develop businesses of women victims of violence;
e. endeavoring to provide capital for women victims of violence; and
f. expanding access to information and promoting products of women victims of violence.
(4) In conducting empowerment of women victims of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government may establish cooperation with job training institutions organized by the private sector.

text:
Pasal 29
(1) Pemerintah Daerah dapat melakukan kerjasama dalam  rangka mencapai tujuan penyelenggaraan perlindungan  perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan.
(2) Kerjasama sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilakukan  dengan:
a. Pemerintah;
b. Pemerintah provinsi;
c. Pemerintah kabupaten/kota lain; dan
d. Lembaga non pemerintah.
(3) Kerjasama sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1), meliputi:  a. Pertukaran data dan informasi;
b. Rehabilitasi korban tindak Kekerasan;
c. Pemulangan dan reintegrasi sosial; dan
d. Penyediaan barang bukti dan saksi dan ditindaklanjuti  sesuai dengan Peraturan Perundang-undangan.
(4) Kerjasama sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (2) dan  ayat (3), dilakukan dalam bentuk Kesepakatan Bersama.

translated_text:
Article 29
(1) Regional Government may conduct cooperation in order to achieve the objectives of implementing protection for women and children victims of violence.
(2) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be conducted with:
a. Government;
b. Provincial government;
c. Other regency/city government; and
d. Non-governmental institutions.
(3) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1), includes:
a. Exchange of data and information;
b. Rehabilitation of victims of acts of Violence;
c. Repatriation and social reintegration; and
d. Provision of evidence and witnesses and followed up in accordance with Laws and Regulations.
(4) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (2) and paragraph (3), shall be conducted in the form of Joint Agreement.
